<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikhail Borisovich of Tver</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1453">1453</a>–<a href="/years/1505">1505</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikhail Borisovich was the last Grand Prince of Tver, from 1461 to 1485. The son of Boris Alexandrovich, he at first allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, joining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> against Novgorod, but when he sought the support of Casimir IV of Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, Ivan besieged Tver in 1485. Mikhail fled to Lithuania, where he died, and Tver was annexed to Moscow.</p></div>
